0066 — a transform origin anywhere, and moving.

The compiler read nine keywords (`origin-top-left`, ...) into
PROP.originX/originY, fractions of the box from its centre, and the props
were documented NOT animatable. A pivot 12 px in from an edge, or 20 px in
from the right whatever width layout gives the box, had no spelling, and a
zoom whose focal point travels had none either.

What it adds:

- `contracts/spec/spec.ts`, regenerated `spec.rs`, the microts spec and
  component types: props `originXPx` (219) and `originYPx` (220), f32 px
  added to the origin the fraction places — CSS's `calc(<percentage> +
  <length>)` per axis, which is what a `<length-percentage>` origin is. The
  origin animates: originX, originY, originXPx, originYPx take anim bits
  73-76 (timeline and `animate()`; no transition bit, as every bit past 31).
- `engine/core/src/style.rs`: the two fields. `draw.rs`: `origin_px`, used
  by the 2D `local_affine` (so hit testing too) and the 3D path alike.
- `framework/compiler/animation.ts`: `parseTransformOrigin`, CSS's 2D
  grammar — one value is x unless it is `top`/`bottom`, two keywords in
  either order, a length or percentage pinned to its position (x first),
  `calc()` adding and subtracting percentages and px; a third value (z) is
  null. `transformOrigin` is a keyframe property that pins all four props in
  every keyframe that writes it, as CSS's computed value is the whole origin;
  `originX`/`originY`/`originXPx`/`originYPx` are keyframe properties by name.
- `framework/compiler/tailwind.ts`: `origin-[x_y]` (`_` for a space) writes
  all four props. A keyword origin writes the fraction alone, as it did, so
  every record that names one is the bytes it was; where another variant of
  the same literal sets a length, the keyword's variant writes it as 0.

Why the origin animates: with rotation and scale held, moving the origin is
a translate by (I - RS) * the move, which a translate track already carries;
with scale moving too it is the PRODUCT of two eased curves, which no eased
translate track carries without being sampled per frame. CSS animates
`transform-origin`; After Effects keys its anchor point. Under a declared
shutter it is sampled between ticks like a translate (0067).

Class `upstream`: a declaration the core turns into the affine every backend
already receives; no target-side change. 0066 sits after `0065` only because
the anim bits are positional.

Guards (`engine/core/src/tests.rs`): `an_origin_length_is_the_fraction_it_equals`
— a 100 px box turned about 25 px in, written three ways (fraction, left
edge plus a length, centre minus a length), is the same words on the 2D and
the 3D path; red with the length left out of `local_affine`, and separately
red with it left out of the 3D path. `an_origin_animates_its_fraction_and_its_length`
— `animate()` on each passes through the quarter-box pivot and lands; red
with the two props not animatable. Vendored `tests/tailwind.test.ts` pins
the compiler: the grammar, what CSS refuses, the variant rule, keyframes.

Ledgers, on `claude/merge-train-3` at 2884e13 (0001-0064) with 0065-0067
on top, against what the train had recorded: all 50 digests and all 58
`visibility` rows match, so no existing entry moves — a keyword origin's
record is the bytes it was. The same held on main at 524173f when this was
0056. `compositions/origin` is new in both: 30 frames, digest 5ed72f55…,
the one first recorded at 524173f; 4 nodes, 4 named, every one shown.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

